            <ArticleTitle>[Adrenal cysts: presentation of 6 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We report six cases of adrenal cyst, a rare pathologic entity which poses diagnostic problems and therapeutic controversies.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We report six cases of adrenal cysts in 4 female and 2 male patients ages 26 to 68 years. All cases underwent surgical treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Pathologic studies showed that all were adrenal cysts without malignancy in any case.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Adrenal cysts are a rare disease of which correct diagnosis is difficult so that many times patients undergo surgery without a proper preoperative diagnosis. There are controversies about the right management of adrenal cysts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
